# SRG-APP-000369-AU-000250  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must be configured to perform audit reduction that
# does not alter original content or time ordering of log records.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000369-AU-000250
group:           V-206502
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-001881
control_rev5:    AU-7

contribution:    Splunk performs audit reduction at search time over the stored rawdata
                 journal, so reduction does not rewrite the stored record; the
                 application's own contribution is to compute and store hashes over the
                 rawdata slices so that any alteration of the stored record is detectable
                 rather than assumed absent.

governs:         indexes.conf - The indexes data is stored in, how large they may grow and how long data
                 is kept.

check:           indexes.conf [<index>] enableDataIntegrityControl in 1|true

external:        Confirming that a given reduction left content and time ordering intact is
                 a comparison of search output against the stored journal, which the
                 assessor performs; the application setting supplies the hash baseline that
                 comparison relies on.
external:        Protecting the index files from modification outside Splunk rests on
                 operating system file permissions and on the storage platform.

citation:        indexes.conf.spec:382-388 [<index>] per-index options, :594
                 enableDataIntegrityControl = <boolean>, :599 "Default: false".
finding:         Assessed at the application layer alone: enableDataIntegrityControl is not
                 enabled on the indexes holding audit records, so Splunk computes no
                 rawdata hashes and the application offers no means of showing that
                 reduction left the stored content unaltered.
